    },
    {
      "id": "X8qhXcrujtMthptrq9Mjq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 447.5078125,
      "y": 775.984375,
      "width": 601.759521484375,
      "height": 160,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1438175069,
      "version": 795,
      "versionNonce": 1718615123,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789657689583,
      "created": 1789655351058,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Non functional Requirements\n* concurrent user searching, let's say 10k ride requests within a city\n* keeping track of location of active rides driver (pinging every 5 seconds)\n* rides matching can take time, so keeping a threshold of 1 second\nfor first driver to match, then if cancels then keep hopping around until list\nexhausts of nearby region\n* drivers can only accept one ride, multiple drivers trying to accept same ride\nwill not be allowed",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Non functional Requirements\n* concurrent user searching, let's say 10k ride requests within a city\n* keeping track of location of active rides driver (pinging every 5 seconds)\n* rides matching can take time, so keeping a threshold of 1 second\nfor first driver to match, then if cancels then keep hopping around until list\nexhausts of nearby region\n* drivers can only accept one ride, multiple drivers trying to accept same ride\nwill not be allowed",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "C50FS3Y8OEEBy6Zkd-4Cx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1200.453125,
      "y": 273.3125,
      "width": 540.1340789794922,
      "height": 560,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1366207261,
      "version": 1680,
      "versionNonce": 672855485,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789658391807,
      "created": 1789656171757,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Estimated Numbers:\nin a city\n10k requests per hour\n100k drivers\n50k total rides in one day\n\nBurst Spike case:\nIn 10 second got 10k requests in peak office hours:\nproblem in gateway, instances handling requests, probably storage\nthrottling\n\nIf the service is in 100 cities, the number multiplies by 100\n\nAs a location service, need a cache instance with geolocation\nindexed with ETA\nWith 100k drivers - sending their location update every 5 seconds,\nthat will be 20k updates per second\n\nin a city of 100, 2M updates/sec globally.\n\nIn this case, we can put a region wise storage, so cities closer to\none region are clubbed together.\nFor example, we can club 5 - 10 cities in one region.\n\nStorage: We need faster reads & frequent writes, so a caching\nstrategy will be better (with replication for durability not for\nreads).\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Estimated Numbers:\nin a city\n10k requests per hour\n100k drivers\n50k total rides in one day\n\nBurst Spike case:\nIn 10 second got 10k requests in peak office hours:\nproblem in gateway, instances handling requests, probably storage throttling\n\nIf the service is in 100 cities, the number multiplies by 100\n\nAs a location service, need a cache instance with geolocation indexed with ETA\nWith 100k drivers - sending their location update every 5 seconds, that will be 20k updates per second\n\nin a city of 100, 2M updates/sec globally.\n\nIn this case, we can put a region wise storage, so cities closer to one region are clubbed together.\nFor example, we can club 5 - 10 cities in one region.\n\nStorage: We need faster reads & frequent writes, so a caching strategy will be better (with replication for durability not for reads).\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
