    {
      "id": "SoYsBjFqKgHUcgQs5-pUP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1873.5281261795692,
      "y": 248.51301906738541,
      "width": 640.9459486515509,
      "height": 440,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 112582525,
      "version": 1188,
      "versionNonce": 1385610429,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789659238856,
      "created": 1789658367872,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cache - Redis\nRedis would be our choice here to create a cluster partitioned by city, indexed\non driver location by ETA.\n\nrider -> requests (lat, long) -> system (searches within 5 KM of lat,long specified)\n-> redis (find_drivers(city, [lat,lng]+5KM) -> returns the list order by\nRouting_service to find ETA -> matching starts based on ranked drivers\n\nIn Peak:\n- One city becomes a hot partition, in this case also the geohasing works as the\nqueries will be on those block sets\n- Partition by cities? Partitioning based on geohasing of city into blocks where\nwe can use the block to identify rider's block and search drivers within those\nblocks.\n- In hot city, where multiple riders are competing for limited drivers, the atomicity\nmatters. In redis we can achieve atomic locking by Lua script, update to\nRESERVED and update to ACCEPTED if RESERVED. The problem, the R1 and\nR2 both offered D1, D1 accepted R1, but R2 offer is still valid.\n How are the offers stored? Offers are stored in another storage where once a\ndriver accepts, the other requests should be declined automatically and a queue\nwill deliver the message to R2 the search continues\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Cache - Redis\nRedis would be our choice here to create a cluster partitioned by city, indexed on driver location by ETA.\n\nrider -> requests (lat, long) -> system (searches within 5 KM of lat,long specified) -> redis (find_drivers(city, [lat,lng]+5KM) -> returns the list order by Routing_service to find ETA -> matching starts based on ranked drivers\n\nIn Peak:\n- One city becomes a hot partition, in this case also the geohasing works as the queries will be on those block sets\n- Partition by cities? Partitioning based on geohasing of city into blocks where we can use the block to identify rider's block and search drivers within those blocks.\n- In hot city, where multiple riders are competing for limited drivers, the atomicity matters. In redis we can achieve atomic locking by Lua script, update to RESERVED and update to ACCEPTED if RESERVED. The problem, the R1 and R2 both offered D1, D1 accepted R1, but R2 offer is still valid.\n How are the offers stored? Offers are stored in another storage where once a driver accepts, the other requests should be declined automatically and a queue will deliver the message to R2 the search continues\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
